  data:  # fef9
    kind: invariant  # fef9
    title: "C++ external dsts carry the calling file comma-joined #include list as their module slot; the coverage gate never expands that disjunction, so no module_completeness entry can match and every C++ repo with system includes is permanently withheld"  # fef9
    status: violated  # fef9
    priority: 1  # fef9
    parent:  # fef9
    tags:  # fef9
    - io_boundary  # fef9
    - verify_claims  # fef9
    - cpp  # fef9
    - false_inconclusive  # fef9
    - node_identity  # fef9
    isbefore: []  # fef9
    duplicate_of: []  # fef9
    not_duplicate_of: []  # fef9
    pr_ref:  # fef9
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-24 while scoping WI-lutuh (the stdlib module_completeness audit).\nIt is a BLOCKER for the C++ half of that scoping: no amount of catalogue\nenumeration can help C++ until this is fixed.\n\nMEASURED on the WI-lutuh sample sweep, unmodified upstream repos, merged dev\n(@dfe3ba8b3e). Artifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/lutuh_scope_08242026/\n\n  repo                ext dsts   comma-joined   pct\n  cpp/libzmq            18,625          4,049   21.7%\n  cpp/plasma-desktop    17,062          6,876   40.3%\n  cpp/shaka-packager    28,278          8,348   29.5%\n  c/qemu-openbios        9,197              0    0.0%\n  c/tmate                7,200              0    0.0%\n  c/fuse-overlayfs       1,345              0    0.0%\n  TOTAL c+cpp           81,711         19,273   23.6%\n\nTHE SHAPE. The PATH slot of a C++ external dst is the CALLING FILE'S ENTIRE\n#include LIST, comma-joined:\n\n  cpp:string,sys/socket.h,ws2tcpip.h:0-0:get_socket_address:external_symbol\n\nlibzmq alone mints 117 distinct comma-bearing pseudo-module paths;\nplasma-desktop 162; shaka-packager 360. C is CLEAN at 0% in all three C repos\nsampled, so this is cpp-specific.\n\nNOT A PRODUCER BUG -- THE PRODUCER IS DELIBERATE AND SAYS SO. cpp.py:1393\n(WI-rupik / WI-mafik) builds a DISJUNCTIVE hint on purpose:\n\n    # ... The semantics is \"this call could be from any of the included\n    # headers\"; downstream consumers may split the module_hint on commas\n    # if they need per-header resolution.\n    module_hint = \",\".join(system_includes)\n\nTHE DEFECT IS THAT THE CONTRACT HAS ONLY ONE CONSUMER OUT OF TWO. The\ndisjunction IS expanded on the CLASSIFICATION path --\nio_boundary._module_hint_candidates (io_boundary.py:2595), called from\nio_boundary.py:916, which splits on commas AND strips header suffixes. It is\nNOT expanded on the COVERAGE-GATE path: verify_claims._uncatalogued_external_\nmodules takes the raw string from _module_from_symbol_path(dst) and hands it\nstraight to IoBoundaryCatalog.module_io_is_enumerated. Verified live:\n\n  module_io_is_enumerated('string,sys/socket.h,ws2tcpip.h')  -> False\n  module_io_is_enumerated('string')                          -> False\n\n_module_hint_candidates has exactly ONE call site in the whole tree.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND NOISE. BoundaryCoverage.qualifying_only is `not unknown`\n(verify_claims.py:2960), so the uncatalogued list must be EXACTLY EMPTY for a\nverdict to stop being withheld. A synthetic name like\n'string,sys/socket.h,ws2tcpip.h' can never appear in any module_completeness\nlist, so every C++ repo that includes system headers is PERMANENTLY withheld --\nenumerating 'string', 'cstring' and 'vector' in cpp.yaml would not move it.\n\nSECOND DAMAGE, NOT MEASURED IN DEPTH: node identity. Each distinct include-list\nCOMBINATION mints its own pseudo-module path, so one logical header is split\nacross many nodes and one node merges symbols from unrelated headers. Same\nclass as INV-rilit, different mechanism.\n\nNOT INVESTIGATED: whether the taint path expands the disjunction; whether any\nother language builds a joined module_hint the same way; the FP/FN trade of\nrouting the gate through _module_hint_candidates (the docstring at\nio_boundary.py:2620 records a measured 3.4% residual FP rate for the\nclassification path's use of it, which is evidence the expansion is sound\nthere but says nothing about the gate)."  # fef9
    fields:  # fef9
      statement: "A module hint the producer builds as a DISJUNCTION must be expanded identically on every consumer path. A C++ external dst carries the calling file entire comma-joined #include list as its module slot; io_boundary._module_hint_candidates expands it for CLASSIFICATION, but verify_claims._uncatalogued_external_modules does not, so the joined string reaches the coverage gate as a synthetic pseudo-module that no module_completeness entry can ever match and every C++ repo with system includes is permanently withheld."  # fef9
      root_cause: "cpp.py:1393 sets module_hint to a comma-join of system_includes deliberately (WI-rupik / WI-mafik), stating in a comment that downstream consumers may split it on commas. That contract is honoured by exactly ONE consumer -- io_boundary._module_hint_candidates (io_boundary.py:2595), whose sole call site is io_boundary.py:916 on the classification path. The coverage gate takes the raw _module_from_symbol_path(dst) string straight to module_io_is_enumerated, so the disjunction is never expanded there. A contract stated in a producer comment is not enforced (LIVE.md rule 7: one fact, two homes -- the second silently wins)."  # fef9
- op: discuss  # 4893
  at: '2026-08-24T23:22:04Z'  # 4893
  by: agent  # 4893
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4893
  clock: 2  # 4893
  nonce: '4893'  # 4893
  message: "RELATIONSHIP TO INV-funuf, recorded so this is not folded as a duplicate and\nnot mistaken for a reopening of it. RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT.\n\nINV-funuf (satisfied, P1) and this item share ONE producer line (cpp.py:1393,\nmodule_hint = \",\".join(system_includes)) and ONE producer comment (\"downstream\nconsumers may split the module_hint on commas\"). They are different items\nbecause that contract has TWO consumers and only one was served.\n\n  INV-funuf   statement: \"a catalogued I/O call site must reach its catalogue\n              entry regardless of how the analyzer spells the module slot\"\n              consumer:  IoBoundaryCatalog.lookup_with_module (CLASSIFICATION)\n              fix:       io_boundary._module_hint_candidates, which DOES split\n                         on commas and DOES strip header suffixes\n              status:    correctly satisfied -- re-read its statement, it is\n                         about catalogue MATCHING and that half works\n\n  INV-zimud   statement: \"a disjunction must be expanded identically on EVERY\n              (this)     consumer path\"\n              consumer:  verify_claims._uncatalogued_external_modules\n                         (COVERAGE GATE)\n              state:     unserved -- it hands the raw _module_from_symbol_path\n                         string straight to module_io_is_enumerated\n              effect:    a WITHHELD verdict, not a missed classification\n\n_module_hint_candidates has exactly ONE call site in the whole tree\n(io_boundary.py:916). That is the shape of the defect: the fix for INV-funuf\nwas correct and complete FOR ITS OWN STATEMENT, and the second consumer was\nnever wired to it.\n\nI am NOT proposing to reopen INV-funuf. Its own statement holds and its own\nrepro (whisper.cpp, 6 of 86 primitives matched) is about the path that now\nworks."  # 4893
